NAME
    setreg - write a value to a processor register

SYNOPSIS
    setreg <register> <value>
    setreg <cpu> <register> <value>

DESCRIPTION
    Writes hexadecimal <value> to <register> on the main processor or on
    the processor named by <cpu> (see cpus(1)). Useful for testing
    alternate branches while halted at a breakpoint or advancing a program
    counter past a spin loop.

    Values are validated against the target register's bit width and
    refused rather than silently truncated if out of range. An unknown
    register name prints the registers available on that processor.

    Only processors advertising 'setreg' in cpus(1) accept register
    writes; read-only processors and read-only individual registers return
    an error. Because only one processor halts at a time, avoid writing
    registers on a coprocessor that is actively executing.

EXAMPLES
    setreg a 0007
    setreg pc 8123
    setreg p 34
    setreg spc a 00
    setreg sa1 x 0010

EXIT STATUS
    0   Register updated (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown or read-only register, out-of-range
        value, unsupported processor, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    regs(1), cpus(1), bp(1), step(1), eval(1)
